{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791433733402,"sessionID":"ses_ee63b6887ffe74gjtaZHK065lF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"campfire_add_finding","callID":"call_00_rzepkudy31o075ims2dl9pg4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"workspaceId":"ws_8ac7734081754950","summary":"Cause: the eu-west-1 POST /orders/submit 503s were caused by route change chg-eu-2048 (rollout-842) at 09:16:42 UTC sending all traffic to checkout-v2-eu, which had zero healthy endpoints because the rollout was paused before EU endpoint registration; the edge returned no_healthy_upstream.","detail":"Convergent evidence. (1) The only edge route change for the endpoint in 09:00-09:24 UTC switched eu-west-1 to checkout-v2-eu at 09:16:42, ~29 s before the first sampled 503 at 09:17:11. (2) checkout-v2-eu had zero registered/healthy endpoints in 09:16-09:30 UTC with rollout-842 paused_before_eu_endpoint_registration at 09:14 UTC, while checkout-v1-eu had six healthy endpoints. (3) All three sampled failures were edge no_healthy_upstream 503s emitted before any checkout-api span, with no database span. (4) The elevated payments DB wait belongs to settlement-export, not checkout-api, so the payments database is not the cause. Confidence high but the evidence set does not include the live rollback or the reason the rollout auto-advanced the route before endpoints registered; that remains unknown.","confidence":0.9,"sourceArtifactId":"art_ece5ac999e3647b2"},"output":"{\n  \"createdBy\": {\n    \"actorId\": \"agt_55bd9c6044454837\",\n    \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n  },\n  \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_48421111760a486f\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:28:53.362Z\",\n  \"id\": \"find_b700efa3c5ba42c3\",\n  \"workspaceId\": \"ws_8ac7734081754950\",\n  \"summary\": \"Cause: the eu-west-1 POST /orders/submit 503s were caused by route change chg-eu-2048 (rollout-842) at 09:16:42 UTC sending all traffic to checkout-v2-eu, which had zero healthy endpoints because the rollout was paused before EU endpoint registration; the edge returned no_healthy_upstream.\",\n  \"detail\": \"Convergent evidence. (1) The only edge route change for the endpoint in 09:00-09:24 UTC switched eu-west-1 to checkout-v2-eu at 09:16:42, ~29 s before the first sampled 503 at 09:17:11. (2) checkout-v2-eu had zero registered/healthy endpoints in 09:16-09:30 UTC with rollout-842 paused_before_eu_endpoint_registration at 09:14 UTC, while checkout-v1-eu had six healthy endpoints. (3) All three sampled failures were edge no_healthy_upstream 503s emitted before any checkout-api span, with no database span. (4) The elevated payments DB wait belongs to settlement-export, not checkout-api, so the payments database is not the cause. Confidence high but the evidence set does not include the live rollback or the reason the rollout auto-advanced the route before endpoints registered; that remains unknown.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"sourceArtifactId\": \"art_ece5ac999e3647b2\",\n  \"currentness\": \"current\"\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1791433733346,"end":1791433733369}},"id":"prt_119c56c2e0018ne9Bi3c9rm35s","sessionID":"ses_ee63b6887ffe74gjtaZHK065lF","messageID":"msg_119c5648f0012aYsCJgPr6DeL0"}}
